From 2791f226ad9205bda6b68a673344621756669b4c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] VideoRenderers: LinuxRendererGL.h includes what its Dolby
 Vision members need

CPictureBuffer of the desktop OpenGL renderer carries a CDVMetadataBuffer and
DVD_NOPTS_VALUE, but the header includes nothing that declares them: a file
that includes LinuxRendererGL.h before the renderer manager (OverlayRendererGL.cpp
does, at its line 12) fails with "'CDVMetadataBuffer' does not name a type".
The GLES header, which carries the same member, includes DVDVideoCodec.h; do
the same here. Only the desktop OpenGL renderer builds from this header, which
the GBM/GLES image does not, so nothing in the image changes.

Tested: a translation unit that includes only LinuxRendererGL.h, compiled with
the flags of the build, fails on the two lines before and compiles after.
---
 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/LinuxRendererGL.h | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/LinuxRendererGL.h b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/LinuxRendererGL.h
index b8aa50f..b2947f3 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/LinuxRendererGL.h
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/LinuxRendererGL.h
@@ -13,6 +13,7 @@
 #include "system_gl.h"
 
 #include "FrameBufferObject.h"
+#include "cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodec.h"
 #include "cores/VideoSettings.h"
 #include "RenderInfo.h"
 #include "BaseRenderer.h"
-- 
2.53.0

